Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd939x: initialize PCM crosstalk with compander bypass

PCM PA startup always enables the crosstalk path, but DAC startup
returns before programming its coefficients when the compander is
disabled. Starting directly in bypass mode therefore leaves the
coefficients at their reset values. Playback that first enabled the
compander inherits its coefficients and hides the missing initialization.

Program the crosstalk coefficients before the compander bypass branch,
so PCM startup does not depend on an earlier compander-enabled stream.
Keep compander thresholds, clocks and reset programming conditional.

---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd939x.c
@@ -535,6 +535,11 @@
 					      WCD939X_REFBUFF_UHQA_CTL_REFBUFN_IOUT_CTL, 1);
 	}
 
+	/* The PCM crosstalk path is enabled even with the compander bypassed. */
+	snd_soc_component_write(component, sec_base + 0, 0x1f);
+	snd_soc_component_write(component, sec_base + 3, 0x4f);
+	snd_soc_component_write(component, sec_base + 2, 0x11);
+
 	if (!comp_en) {
 		/* compander bypassed, gain from register */
 		if (hphr)
@@ -583,11 +588,6 @@
 	else
 		snd_soc_component_write_field(component, WCD939X_DIGITAL_CDC_COMP_CTL_0,
 					      WCD939X_CDC_COMP_CTL_0_HPHL_COMP_EN, true);
-
-	/* crosstalk coefficients (stock: scale 0x1f, sec2/3 0x11/0x4f) */
-	snd_soc_component_write(component, sec_base + 0, 0x1f);
-	snd_soc_component_write(component, sec_base + 3, 0x4f);
-	snd_soc_component_write(component, sec_base + 2, 0x11);
 }
 
 static void wcd939x_hph_pcm_post_dac(struct snd_soc_component *component)
